# Code owners: the files whose change can do harm that no later check would
# catch (the owner's review criteria 1 to 8). Every other file is
# unowned: an agent pull request touching only those merges on the reviewer
# App's approval. There is deliberately no catch-all line, and none may be added.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching line. So each kept directory is listed first,
# the documents, tests, lockfiles and pins inside it that are released follow
# with no owner, and the owner's own words, the rules and the workflows come
# after those so they win. The five template lines of branchLeft/standards
# (SYNC-1) are the final lines of the file.
#
# Check an edit with the codeowners/errors API: an empty list is the only signal
# that every entry resolved. A directory whose scripts a secret-bearing job runs
# is owned whole (a new file there would otherwise shadow a module those scripts
# import), and only named files inside it are released, last. A Dockerfile, its
# .dockerignore and what it copies and runs are owned where such a job builds
# it. infra/provisioning/scripts/test_codeowners_ownership.py fails if not.

